.TH WMSOUNDD 1 "2026" "Window Maker"
.SH NAME
wmsoundd \- Window Maker sound event player daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmsoundd
[\fB\-s\fR\ \fISOCKET\fR] [\fB\-d\fR\ \fIDISPLAY\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.br
.B wmsoundd
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR
.br
.B wmsoundd
\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmsoundd
subscribes to Window Maker's WIPC sound event stream and plays the sound
file mapped to each event in the
.B WMSound
defaults domain. It runs as a user-started daemon, linking libWUtil,
libsndfile and PipeWire, with no X11 dependency.
.PP
Window Maker emits
.B sound
IPC events on its AF_UNIX socket when window actions occur (shading,
iconifying, docking, etc.) and on lifecycle events (startup, shutdown,
workspace switch).
.B wmsoundd
receives these events, looks up the corresponding sound file in the
.B WMSound
domain, and plays it through PipeWire.
.PP
The
.B WMSound
domain maps CamelCase event keys to file names (or
.IR None ).
Sound files are resolved by walking the
.B SoundPath
array, expanding each entry with
.IR wexpandpath (3),
and returning the first
.IR access (2)
hit. Absolute paths are used as-is.
.PP
If the Window Maker IPC socket is not present when
.B wmsoundd
starts, or the connection is dropped or refused, it retries with
exponential backoff and gives up after 10 minutes, exiting with
status 1 (see
.BR "EXIT STATUS" ).
.PP
Sound files are decoded with libsndfile (WAV, AIFF, AU, FLAC,
Ogg/Vorbis, Ogg/Opus, MP3) to 16-bit PCM. Files larger than 16 MiB, or
decoding to more than 64 MiB of PCM, are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " DISPLAY"
Resolve the Window Maker IPC socket for
.I DISPLAY
instead of
.BR $DISPLAY .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print runtime diagnostics to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BI \-s " SOCKET"
Connect to
.I SOCKET
instead of the resolved IPC path.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Used to resolve the Window Maker IPC socket when
.B \-s
is not given.
.TP
.B WMAKER_IPC_SOCKET
Overrides the Window Maker IPC socket path.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the
.B WMSound
domain from disk.
.TP
.B SIGTERM , SIGINT
Stop the IPC session, drain active playback (bounded to 10 seconds)
and exit with status 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean exit on SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure, or give-up after 10 minutes without a usable IPC
socket.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/WindowMaker/WMSound
XDG location for the
.B WMSound
defaults domain.
.TP
.I ~/GNUstep/Defaults/WMSound
Legacy location for the
.B WMSound
defaults domain.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/WindowMaker/Sounds
User sound file directory on the XDG layout, searched first.
.TP
.I ~/GNUstep/Library/WindowMaker/Sounds
User sound file directory on the legacy layout, also searched before
the system path.
.TP
.I /usr/share/WindowMaker/Sounds
System-wide sound file directory, searched last.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR wmaker (1),
.BR wmakermsg (1)
